# Cursor Rules for ChartDB Development

## Code Style
- Follow existing TypeScript conventions in the codebase
- Use functional components with React hooks
- Maintain consistent indentation (4 spaces)
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Add JSDoc comments for complex functions

## Testing
- Write unit tests for new features
- Follow existing test patterns in `__tests__` directories
- Use descriptive test names
- Ensure all tests pass before committing

## Git Workflow
- Make focused commits with clear messages
- Commit format: `type: description` (e.g., `feat: add SurrealDB support`)
- Push changes after completing each logical unit of work
- Work on the designated feature branch

## Database Integration Guidelines
- Follow the existing pattern for database type definitions
- Each database needs: type definition, data types, import/export logic
- Add appropriate test coverage for new database types
- Update documentation for new database support

## Architecture Patterns
- Use existing context providers pattern for state management
- Follow the lib/domain structure for core domain models
- Keep components small and focused
- Separate business logic from UI components
